  "violations": [
    "Page 3, 'Action Items': 'There were no significant issues in your water system in 2025, and we have no recommended action items for our customers in this area.' Page 3 also states: 'In this system in 2025, we conducted 13,657 tests on 2,040 water samples for 225 constituents. We are pleased to confirm that we met every primary and secondary federal and state water quality standard last year.'",
    "Page 14 footnote 3 (Iron): 'In one sample in the Los Altos Suburban system, iron exceeded the SMCL of 300 ppb; however, compliance with the SMCL is based on an RAA, which is less than the SMCL. We are monitoring the levels to confirm we do not exceed the RAA.' (range ND–620 ppb, groundwater)",
    "Page 13 footnote 2 (Nitrate as N, groundwater): average 4.1 ppm with a maximum of 7.8 ppm against the 10 ppm MCL; 'We are closely monitoring the nitrate levels', followed by the infant/pregnancy health advisory language.",
    "Page 15: groundwater PFHxS range ND–4.1 ppt against the 3 ppt notification level (average ND, 'In Compliance: Yes'). Page 10: active sources are in compliance with current California response levels based on running annual averages."
  ],
  "extraction_notes": "Tables on pages 13-15. Per-source columns printed: 'Groundwater' and 'Valley Water' (radiological, inorganic, secondary and notification-level tables); 'Distribution System-Wide' (coliform, lead/copper, DBPs, disinfectant); 'Valley Water' only (surface-water turbidity and TOC); and 'Groundwater' / 'Surface Water' in the unregulated/UCMR table, where 'Surface Water' is the same purchased Valley Water supply under a different heading. No SFPUC/Hetch Hetchy column exists in the 2025 report (footnote 1 says Valley Water deliveries may have included SFPUC water via the interconnection). Cells printed N/A for a source column got no entry (one entry per analyte per column that has data). Each table says 'Contaminants not detected (ND) are not listed', so no explicit ND rows exist beyond Color/Odor groundwater and lead. Anomalies copied as printed: boron is a ppm row (NL 1) but its Valley Water values 120–152/130 are evidently ppb; specific conductance unit printed 'US'; the 'Turbidity (groundwater)' row also carries Valley Water values. 'In Compliance' was Yes for every regulated row. Convention: a range printed 'ND - x' or '<n - x' is stored range_low 0 / range_high x (the printed string is kept in notes). Rows whose Average (or 90th percentile) is printed 'ND' or '<n' but whose range shows a detection are stored value null, average null, detected true, value_basis 'average (printed ND)' - nothing is substituted for the unprintable average. Rows printed ND with no range are detected false. 'sample_year' is the latest year when the report prints a year range; the printed range is in notes."
}
